    {
      "paperId": "/chapter/10.1007/978-981-15-9199-0_13",
      "doi": "10.1007/978-981-15-9199-0_13",
      "title": "A Data-Driven Approach to Anomaly Detection and Health Monitoring for Artificial Satellites",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Takehisa Yairi, Yusuke Fukushima, ... Yukihito Yamaguchi"
        }
      ],
      "year": 2021,
      "abstract": "In the operation of artificial satellites, overall health monitoring of the system and detection of symptoms of potential troubles are very important. For about twenty years, we have studied the data-driven health monitoring methods for artificial satellites, in which machine learning techniques are applied to the house-keeping data of satellites. In this paper, we review the basic of anomaly detection based on unsupervised learning and some results in early studies and then discuss the lessons learned and challenges to be tackled in the data-driven health monitoring for artificial satellites.",
