    {
      "paperId": "/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-39214-6_17",
      "doi": "10.1007/978-3-031-39214-6_17",
      "title": "An Overview of the Space Servicing Requirements in a Sustainable Space Age",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Pablo Lopez Negro, Daniele Filippetto, ... Xiu Tian Yan"
        }
      ],
      "year": 2024,
      "abstract": "Space-based services are flourishing motivated by new needs in fields like communication, navigation and Earth observation. The increasing demand for space infrastructure has stimulated the deployment of innovative technological solutions; however, among the latest developments, on-orbit servicing of spacecraft is not yet implemented in most commercial programs. This chapter explores the opportunities for developing a sustainable and economically viable solution based on on-orbit servicing to extend spacecraft life-time and to reconfigure its main payloads to adapt to new needs. The investigation starts by an analysis of the demand of space based solutions and the prospects for the following years. Then, a discussion about the new developments in space infrastructure is proposed, presenting two alternative concepts: large constellations and on-orbit servicing. Attention is drawn to the latter, discussing the main technological evolutions needed to sustain its implementation. The last section proposes a roadmap for the development and progressive application of the new technologies, aiming at implementing on-orbit servicing on a regular basis for commercial spacecraft.",
      "abstract_not_available": false,
      "snippet": "Space-based services are flourishing motivated by new needs in fields like communication, navigationNavigation \\b and Earth observation. The...",
